---
description: Library Result (no unwrap), small public API, recorded argv only, no SDK/secrets in git.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Production-ready and small

Library paths return `Result`. No `unwrap` / `expect` / `panic!` in non-test library code. Errors name what failed. Tests may unwrap. Delete unused helpers in the same change.

Public API stays small and named after domain concepts (`UidCrc`, `SisField`, `SisPackage`). Do not `pub use` intermediates, crate-private helpers, or a `util` module.

If a crate is already in `Cargo.toml` (e.g. `sha1`), use it. Do not hand-roll a parallel digest.

```rust
// DON'T (non-test library)
std::fs::read(path).unwrap()
fn sha1(data: &[u8]) -> [u8; 20] { /* local loop */ }

// DO
std::fs::read(path).map_err(|e| Error::Other(format!("read {path:?}: {e}")))?
sha1::Sha1::digest(data)
```

## Tests and blobs

Default `cargo test` pins frozen experiment bytes (hex includes / literals). Do not read `.sis` / `.sisx` from disk by default. Do not spawn Wine in default tests.

Never curl, vendor, or commit SDK, ROM, `.sis`, `.sisx`, `.cer`, `.key`.

## Never invent argv

`uidcrc.exe` / `makesis.exe` / `signsis.exe` / `makekeys.exe` / `elf2e32` take recorded tokens only. If a flag was not observed, do not add it.
